  "estimatedMinutes": 2,
  "statement": "Square \\(EFGH\\) has one vertex on each side of square \\(ABCD.\\) Point \\(E\\) is on \\(\\overline{AB}\\) with \\(AE=7\\cdot EB.\\) What is the ratio of the area of \\(EFGH\\) to the area of \\(ABCD?\\)",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{49}{64}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{25}{32}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac78\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{5\\sqrt{2}}{8}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{\\sqrt{14}}{4}\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "b",
    "value": "25/32"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-10a-2011-p11.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Let \\(x = EB.\\) Then \\(AB = 8x.\\) Applying the Pythagorean Theorem to a side of \\(EFGH,\\) we get \\[ \\sqrt{(7x)^2 + x^2} = \\sqrt{50x^2} \\]\n\nThe desired ratio is then \\[ \\dfrac{\\sqrt{50x^2}^2}{(8x)^2} = \\dfrac{50}{64} = \\dfrac{25}{32}. \\]\n\nThus, B is the correct answer.",
      "hints": [
        "Let \\(EB=x\\), so \\(AB=8x\\)",
        "A side of the inner square is the hypotenuse of a \\(7x\\)-by-\\(x\\) triangle"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
